text:
Shady the lane where the wild flower grows;
Scented the air from the wild hedge rose;
Shadows of leaves with the sunlight play;
Vibrant the air with the song birds lay.
What of the maid where the gateway opes,
The wheelman's whistle down the slopes?
Curved is the stream in the distant field;
Solemn the bell in the steeple peaed
Watchful the hunter blowing his horn;
Pped all the quail in the field of corn.
What will the maid to the wheemsn say,
The wheelman waiting his yea nay?
Love is theme for the rustic air;
PASSIONS romance thTobs it's widest there;
Stars of the night and orb of the day
Blend in harmonies of natures sway.
What of the maid by the moss grown gate?
wheelman's joy-he has learned his fate.
